{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0F0A", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:85d11e6570bc9ad3c96b85b3214145a94aac3ffddddf3e3405073dbc4f4906b2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we discuss some more or less immediate\nconsequences of the smooth base change theorem.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0d97175c5ee69c3f4930f4cdcec6b3db272cc8a32b0355bbf9ca7ae921bd4af5", "unit_id": "tag:0F0A:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0F0A", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$L/K$", "MATH_0002": "$g : T \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$K$", "MATH_0004": "$g_L : T_L \\to S_L$", "MATH_0005": "$g$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Spec(L)$", "MATH_0007": "$E \\in D^+(T_\\etale)$", "MATH_0008": "$K$", "MATH_0009": "$E_L$", "MATH_0010": "$E$", "MATH_0011": "$(T_L)_\\etale$", "MATH_0012": "$Rg_{L, *}E_L$", "MATH_0013": "$Rg_*E$", "MATH_0014": "$S_L$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-field-extension}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:98d9c0d0bc6108aeb0b36900c8143983a23bb9e1e70717e2bdcf628ce729b1b0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f30e6d5dfc110094dabfdac7d7ea441b8f0fd1b06f32396b6b9408eba63a830a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an extension of fields. Let <MATH_0002> be a quasi-compact\nand quasi-separated morphism of schemes over <MATH_0003>. Denote\n<MATH_0004> the base change of <MATH_0005> to <MATH_0006>.\nLet <MATH_0007> have cohomology sheaves whose stalks\nare torsion of orders invertible in <MATH_0008>. Let <MATH_0009> be the\npullback of <MATH_0010> to <MATH_0011>. Then\n<MATH_0012> is the pullback of <MATH_0013> to <MATH_0014>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6ea65a71d5e60538625da9c9dc575622870171d22fec7ffd1b073d70bcf3f400", "unit_id": "tag:0F1C:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0F0A", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$L/K$", "MATH_0002": "$L$", "MATH_0003": "$K$", "MATH_0004": "$K'$", "MATH_0005": "$L'$", "MATH_0006": "$K$", "MATH_0007": "$L$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Spec(K') \\to \\Spec(K)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Spec(L') \\to \\Spec(L)$", "MATH_0010": "$K'/K$", "MATH_0011": "$L'/L$", "MATH_0012": "$(T_{K'})_\\etale = T_\\etale$", "MATH_0013": "$(S_{K'})_\\etale = S_\\etale$", "MATH_0014": "$(T_{L'})_\\etale = (T_L)\\etale$", "MATH_0015": "$(S_{L'})_\\etale = (S_L)_\\etale$", "MATH_0016": "$L'/K'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-colimit-syntomic}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-base-change-general}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-definition-perfection}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-p-ring-map}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{proposition-topological-invariance}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{algebra-definition-perfect}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:af9152699d9c802d06ae9467c5948086f04adeadb52a1cbe9fef836fec98ec7b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a2133796f21462c0638801f6c5adc9537f66569310833837a58da8fbef29f2e9", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is separable, then <MATH_0002> is a filtered colimit of smooth\n<MATH_0003>-algebras, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThus the lemma in this case follows immediately from\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nIn the general case, let <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> be the perfect closures\n(Algebra, Definition <REF_0003>)\nof <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007>. Then <MATH_0008> and\n<MATH_0009> are universal homeomorphisms\nas <MATH_0010> and <MATH_0011> are purely inseparable\n(see Algebra, Lemma <REF_0004>).\nThus we have <MATH_0012>,\n<MATH_0013>,\n<MATH_0014>, and\n<MATH_0015> by\nthe topological invariance of <ACCENT_0001>tale cohomology, see\nProposition <REF_0005>.\nThis reduces the lemma to the case of the field\nextension <MATH_0016> which is separable (by definition of\nperfect fields, see Algebra, Definition <REF_0006>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4131d3754288e59f29a73d7a7746ebfdce8d2b4cabfef9ad72a1b271089f2be3", "unit_id": "tag:0F1C:proof"}
